IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc14-part122-forfeiture.l4 -- PART XII.2 "Proceeds of Crime", ss 462.37 to 462.46 (forfeiture; orders; restoration; appeals; suspension; copies) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`), `daydate`, and the keel's definitions (`ccc-definitions`) for the one enumeration `s 2 form of the charge`.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).
-- Provisions that address only a court or the Attorney General are encoded for what they decide; the seat layer asks them from the position of the offender or the person whose property is in question.

§ `PART XII.2 -- Proceeds of Crime: forfeiture (ss 462.37 to 462.46)`

§§ `s 462.37 -- Order of forfeiture of property`

-- src:8207 | 462.37 (1) Subject to this section and sections 462.39 to 462.41, if an offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of a designated offence and the court imposing sentence on or discharging the offender, on application of the Attorney General, is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that any property is proceeds of crime obtained through the commission of the designated offence, the court shall order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law.
@ref s 462.37(1) (src:8207)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court imposing sentence on or discharging the offender is acting on application of the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is proceeds of crime obtained through the commission of the designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the court imposing sentence on or discharging the offender is acting on application of the Attorney General`
            AND `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is proceeds of crime obtained through the commission of the designated offence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of a designated offence and the court imposing sentence on or discharging the offender, on application of the Attorney General, is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities"
    ELSE `the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("if" unmet); NOTHING when "designated offence" is itself not covered

-- src:8209 | (2) If the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that property in respect of which an order of forfeiture would otherwise be made under subsection (1) was obtained through the commission of the designated offence of which the offender is convicted or discharged, but the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is proceeds of crime, the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to that property.
@ref s 462.37(2) (src:8209)
GIVEN `an order of forfeiture would otherwise be made under subsection (1) in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that the property was obtained through the commission of the designated offence of which the offender is convicted or discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to the property` MEANS
    IF `an order of forfeiture would otherwise be made under subsection (1) in respect of the property`
        AND `the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that the property was obtained through the commission of the designated offence of which the offender is convicted or discharged`
        AND `the court is satisfied, beyond a reasonable doubt, that the property is proceeds of crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the evidence does not establish to the satisfaction of the court that property in respect of which an order of forfeiture would otherwise be made under subsection (1) was obtained through the commission of the designated offence"

-- src:8211 | (2.01) A court imposing sentence on an offender convicted of an offence described in subsection (2.02) shall, on application of the Attorney General and subject to this section and sections 462.4 and 462.41, order that any property of the offender that is identified by the Attorney General in the application be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that
-- src:8212 | (a) within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, the offender engaged in a pattern of criminal activity for the purpose of directly or indirectly receiving a material benefit, including a financial benefit; or
-- src:8213 | (b) the income of the offender from sources unrelated to designated offences cannot reasonably account for the value of all the property of the offender.
@ref s 462.37(2.01) (src:8211-8213)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence described in subsection (2.02), by s 462.37(2.02)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property of the offender is identified by the Attorney General in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, the offender engaged in a pattern of criminal activity for the purpose of directly or indirectly receiving a material benefit, including a financial benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the income of the offender from sources unrelated to designated offences cannot reasonably account for the value of all the property of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is made by the Attorney General` AND `the property of the offender is identified by the Attorney General in the application`
            AND (`the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, the offender engaged in a pattern of criminal activity for the purpose of directly or indirectly receiving a material benefit, including a financial benefit`   -- (a)
                 OR `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the income of the offender from sources unrelated to designated offences cannot reasonably account for the value of all the property of the offender`))   -- (b)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that"
    ELSE `the offender is convicted of an offence described in subsection (2.02), by s 462.37(2.02)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when (2.02) is itself not covered

-- "within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced": the period is counted back ten years from the day the proceedings were commenced (the Interpretation Act is not among the sources).
@ref s 462.37(2.01)(a) (src:8212)
GIVEN `the date the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced` IS A DATE
      `the date of the pattern of criminal activity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.01)(a) the pattern of criminal activity is within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced` MEANS
    IF `the date of the pattern of criminal activity` AT MOST `the date the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced`
        AND `the date of the pattern of criminal activity` AT LEAST Date (DATE_DAY `the date the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced`) (DATE_MONTH `the date the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced`) (DATE_YEAR `the date the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced` MINUS 10)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced in respect of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced"

-- src:8215 | (2.02) The offences are the following:
-- src:8216 | (a) a criminal organization offence punishable by five or more years of imprisonment;
-- src:8217 | (b) an offence under section 5, 6 or 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act — or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to an offence under any of those sections — prosecuted by indictment;
-- src:8218 | (c) an offence under subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act — or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to an offence under any of those subsections — prosecuted by indictment; and
-- src:8219 | (d) an offence under any of sections 279.01 to 279.03.
@ref s 462.37(2.02) (src:8215-8219)
GIVEN `the offence is a criminal organization offence, by s 2 criminal organization offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the maximum imprisonment of the offence, its indictable limb or its only limb` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the offence is under section 5, 6 or 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form the charge takes` IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is the section of the Code asked about` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.02) the offence is an offence described in subsection (2.02)` MEANS
    IF (`the form the charge takes` EQUALS `the offence itself` AND `the offence is the section of the Code asked about`'s `section` AT LEAST 279.01 AND `the offence is the section of the Code asked about`'s `section` AT MOST 279.03)   -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the form the charge takes` EQUALS `a form of participation that is none of those`)) AND `the offence is prosecuted by indictment`
                AND (`the offence is under section 5, 6 or 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` OR `the offence is under subsection 9(1) or (2), 10(1) or (2), 11(1) or (2), 12(1), (4), (5), (6) or (7), 13(1) or 14(1) of the Cannabis Act`)   -- (b), (c)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the offence is a criminal organization offence, by s 2 criminal organization offence`   -- (a)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a criminal organization offence is itself not covered
              WHEN JUST c THEN
                  IF c
                  THEN (CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment of the offence, its indictable limb or its only limb`
                        WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence section states no maximum, so "five or more years of imprisonment" cannot be tested here
                        WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
                        WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` longest THEN
                            IF (longest's years TIMES 12 PLUS longest's months) AT LEAST 60 AND NOT (longest's `less a day` AND (longest's years TIMES 12 PLUS longest's months) EQUALS 60 AND longest's days EQUALS 0)
                            THEN JUST TRUE
                            ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a criminal organization offence punishable by five or more years of imprisonment"
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offences are the following"

-- src:8221 | (2.03) A court shall not make an order of forfeiture under subsection (2.01) in respect of any property that the offender establishes, on a balance of probabilities, is not proceeds of crime.
@ref s 462.37(2.03) (src:8221)
GIVEN `the offender establishes, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is not proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.03) the court is barred from making an order of forfeiture under subsection (2.01) in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the offender establishes, on a balance of probabilities, that the property is not proceeds of crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any property that the offender establishes, on a balance of probabilities, is not proceeds of crime"

DECLARE `s 462.37(2.04) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.37(2.04)(a) the circumstances of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced`
    `s 462.37(2.04)(b) any act or omission, other than one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, was committed by the offender and constitutes an offence punishable by indictment under any Act of Parliament`
    `s 462.37(2.04)(c) any act or omission that the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, was committed by the offender and is an offence in the place where it was committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute an offence punishable by indictment under any Act of Parliament`
    `s 462.37(2.04)(d) any other factor that the court considers relevant`
    `s 462.37(2.04) a matter that the court does not consider relevant`

-- src:8223 | (2.04) In determining whether the offender has engaged in a pattern of criminal activity described in paragraph (2.01)(a), the court shall consider
-- src:8224 | (a) the circumstances of the offence for which the offender is being sentenced;
-- src:8225 | (b) any act or omission — other than an act or omission that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced — that the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, was committed by the offender and constitutes an offence punishable by indictment under any Act of Parliament;
-- src:8226 | (c) any act or omission that the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, was committed by the offender and is an offence in the place where it was committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute an offence punishable by indictment under any Act of Parliament; and
-- src:8227 | (d) any other factor that the court considers relevant.
@ref s 462.37(2.04) (src:8223-8227)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 462.37(2.04) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.04) the court must consider the matter in determining whether the offender has engaged in a pattern of criminal activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 462.37(2.04) a matter that the court does not consider relevant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other factor that the court considers relevant"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8229 | (2.05) A court shall not determine that an offender has engaged in a pattern of criminal activity unless the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender committed, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a),
-- src:8230 | (a) acts or omissions — other than an act or omission that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced — that constitute at least two serious offences or one criminal organization offence;
-- src:8231 | (b) acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute at least two serious offences or one criminal organization offence; or
-- src:8232 | (c) an act or omission described in paragraph (a) that constitutes a serious offence and an act or omission described in paragraph (b) that, if committed in Canada, would constitute a serious offence.
@ref s 462.37(2.05) (src:8229-8232)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, of the commission, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a), of the acts or omissions below` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of acts or omissions, other than the one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that constitute serious offences, by s 2 serious offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of acts or omissions, other than the one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that constitute criminal organization offences, by s 2 criminal organization offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute serious offences` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute criminal organization offences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.05) the court is barred from determining that the offender has engaged in a pattern of criminal activity` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, of the commission, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a), of the acts or omissions below`
        AND (`the number of acts or omissions, other than the one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that constitute serious offences, by s 2 serious offence` AT LEAST 2
             OR `the number of acts or omissions, other than the one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that constitute criminal organization offences, by s 2 criminal organization offence` AT LEAST 1)   -- (a)
        OR (`the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, of the commission, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a), of the acts or omissions below`
            AND (`the number of acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute serious offences` AT LEAST 2
                 OR `the number of acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute criminal organization offences` AT LEAST 1))   -- (b)
        OR (`the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, of the commission, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a), of the acts or omissions below`
            AND `the number of acts or omissions, other than the one that constitutes the offence for which the offender is being sentenced, that constitute serious offences, by s 2 serious offence` AT LEAST 1
            AND `the number of acts or omissions that are offences in the place where they were committed and, if committed in Canada, would constitute serious offences` AT LEAST 1)   -- (c)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court shall not determine that an offender has engaged in a pattern of criminal activity unless the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the offender committed, within the period referred to in paragraph (2.01)(a)" (the unless is met, so the bar does not apply)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8234 | (2.06) Nothing in subsection (2.01) shall be interpreted as preventing the Attorney General from making an application under subsection (1) in respect of any property.
@ref s 462.37(2.06) (src:8234)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (1) in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.06) subsection (2.01) prevents the Attorney General from making the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection (1) in respect of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (2.01) shall be interpreted as preventing the Attorney General from making an application under subsection (1) in respect of any property"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application under subsection (1)"

-- src:8236 | (2.07) A court may, if it considers it in the interests of justice, decline to make an order of forfeiture against any property that would otherwise be subject to forfeiture under subsection (2.01). The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref s 462.37(2.07) (src:8236)
GIVEN `the property would otherwise be subject to forfeiture under subsection (2.01)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.07) the court may decline to make an order of forfeiture against the property` MEANS
    IF `the property would otherwise be subject to forfeiture under subsection (2.01)` AND `the court considers it in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court may, if it considers it in the interests of justice, decline to make an order of forfeiture"

@ref s 462.37(2.07) (src:8236)
GIVEN `the court declined to make an order of forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.07) the court must give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court declined to make an order of forfeiture`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

-- src:8238 | (2.1) An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 462.37(2.1) (src:8238)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(2.1) an order may be issued in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:8240 | (3) If a court is satisfied that an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) or (2.01) should be made in respect of any property of an offender but that the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot be made subject to an order, the court may, instead of ordering the property or any part of or interest in the property to be forfeited, order the offender to pay a fine in an amount equal to the value of the property or the part of or interest in the property. In particular, a court may order the offender to pay a fine if the property or any part of or interest in the property
-- src:8241 | (a) cannot, on the exercise of due diligence, be located;
-- src:8242 | (b) has been transferred to a third party;
-- src:8243 | (c) is located outside Canada;
-- src:8244 | (d) has been substantially diminished in value or rendered worthless; or
-- src:8245 | (e) has been commingled with other property that cannot be divided without difficulty.
@ref s 462.37(3) (src:8240-8245)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) or (2.01) should be made in respect of the property of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot be made subject to an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot, on the exercise of due diligence, be located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been transferred to a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property is located outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been substantially diminished in value or rendered worthless` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been commingled with other property that cannot be divided without difficulty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(3) the court may order the offender to pay a fine instead of ordering the property to be forfeited` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) or (2.01) should be made in respect of the property of the offender`
        AND (`the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot be made subject to an order`
             OR `the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot, on the exercise of due diligence, be located`   -- (a)
             OR `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been transferred to a third party`   -- (b)
             OR `the property or any part of or interest in the property is located outside Canada`   -- (c)
             OR `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been substantially diminished in value or rendered worthless`   -- (d)
             OR `the property or any part of or interest in the property has been commingled with other property that cannot be divided without difficulty`)   -- (e)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a court is satisfied that an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) or (2.01) should be made in respect of any property of an offender but that the property or any part of or interest in the property cannot be made subject to an order, the court may"

@ref s 462.37(3) (src:8240)
GIVEN `the value of the property or the part of or interest in the property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Fine
`s 462.37(3) the amount of the fine` MEANS `a fine of` `the value of the property or the part of or interest in the property`   -- "a fine in an amount equal to the value of the property or the part of or interest in the property"

DECLARE `s 462.37(4) band` HAS
    `minimum` IS AN Imprisonment
    `maximum` IS AN Imprisonment

-- The seven bands of paragraph (a), each in the units the text uses. "does not exceed" puts an amount equal to a threshold in the lower band.
-- src:8247 | (4) Where a court orders an offender to pay a fine pursuant to subsection (3), the court shall
-- src:8248 | (a) impose, in default of payment of that fine, a term of imprisonment
-- src:8249 | (i) not exceeding six months, where the amount of the fine does not exceed ten thousand dollars,
-- src:8250 | (ii) of not less than six months and not exceeding twelve months, where the amount of the fine exceeds ten thousand dollars but does not exceed twenty thousand dollars,
-- src:8251 | (iii) of not less than twelve months and not exceeding eighteen months, where the amount of the fine exceeds twenty thousand dollars but does not exceed fifty thousand dollars,
-- src:8252 | (iv) of not less than eighteen months and not exceeding two years, where the amount of the fine exceeds fifty thousand dollars but does not exceed one hundred thousand dollars,
-- src:8253 | (v) of not less than two years and not exceeding three years, where the amount of the fine exceeds one hundred thousand dollars but does not exceed two hundred and fifty thousand dollars,
-- src:8254 | (vi) of not less than three years and not exceeding five years, where the amount of the fine exceeds two hundred and fifty thousand dollars but does not exceed one million dollars, or
-- src:8255 | (vii) of not less than five years and not exceeding ten years, where the amount of the fine exceeds one million dollars; and
@ref s 462.37(4)(a) (src:8247-8255)
GIVEN `the amount of the fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (`s 462.37(4) band`)
`s 462.37(4)(a) the term of imprisonment to be imposed in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak of a fine of nothing or less
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 10_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `no imprisonment is stated`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 6, 0, FALSE))   -- (i)
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 20_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 6, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 12, 0, FALSE))   -- (ii)
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 50_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 12, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 18, 0, FALSE))   -- (iii)
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 100_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 18, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE))   -- (iv)
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 250_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE))   -- (v)
        IF `the amount of the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 1_000_000 THEN JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE))   -- (vi)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`s 462.37(4) band` OF `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE))   -- (vii)

-- src:8256 | (b) direct that the term of imprisonment imposed pursuant to paragraph (a) be served consecutively to any other term of imprisonment imposed on the offender or that the offender is then serving.
@ref s 462.37(4)(b) (src:8256)
GIVEN `the court orders an offender to pay a fine pursuant to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(4)(b) the term of imprisonment in default is to be served consecutively to any other term of imprisonment imposed on the offender or that the offender is then serving` MEANS
    IF `the court orders an offender to pay a fine pursuant to subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a court orders an offender to pay a fine pursuant to subsection (3), the court shall"

-- src:8258 | (5) Section 736 does not apply to an offender against whom a fine is imposed pursuant to subsection (3).
@ref s 462.37(5) (src:8258)
GIVEN `a fine is imposed on the offender pursuant to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.37(5) section 736 does not apply to the offender` MEANS
    IF `a fine is imposed on the offender pursuant to subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to an offender against whom a fine is imposed pursuant to subsection (3)"

§§ `s 462.371 -- Definition of order; execution; filing of orders from another province`

-- src:8260 | 462.371 (1) In this section, order means an order made under section 462.37 or 462.38.
@ref s 462.371(1) (src:8260)
GIVEN `the provision the order was made under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(1) order` MEANS
    IF `the provision the order was made under`'s `section` EQUALS 462.37 OR `the provision the order was made under`'s `section` EQUALS 462.38
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "order means an order made under section 462.37 or 462.38"

-- src:8262 | (2) An order may be executed anywhere in Canada.
@ref s 462.371(2) (src:8262)
GIVEN `the order is an order within section 462.371(1), by s 462.371(1) order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(2) the order may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order within section 462.371(1), by s 462.371(1) order` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order may be executed anywhere in Canada"

-- src:8264 | (3) Where the Attorney General of a province in which property that is the subject of an order made in another province is situated receives a certified copy of the order and files it with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated, the order shall be entered as a judgment of that court.
@ref s 462.371(3) (src:8264)
GIVEN `the property that is the subject of an order made in another province is situated in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of that province receives a certified copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General files it with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(3) the order is to be entered as a judgment of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the property that is the subject of an order made in another province is situated in the province` AND `the Attorney General of that province receives a certified copy of the order` AND `the Attorney General files it with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Attorney General of a province in which property that is the subject of an order made in another province is situated receives a certified copy of the order and files it"

-- src:8266 | (4) Where the Attorney General of Canada receives a certified copy of an order made in a province in respect of property situated in another province and files the order with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated, the order shall be entered as a judgment of that court.
@ref s 462.371(4) (src:8266)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada receives a certified copy of an order made in a province in respect of property situated in another province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada files the order with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(4) the order is to be entered as a judgment of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada receives a certified copy of an order made in a province in respect of property situated in another province` AND `the Attorney General of Canada files the order with the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the property is situated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Attorney General of Canada receives a certified copy of an order made in a province in respect of property situated in another province and files the order"

-- src:8268 | (5) An order has, from the date it is filed in a court of a province under subsection (3) or (4), the same effect as if it had been an order originally made by that court.
@ref s 462.371(5) (src:8268)
GIVEN `the order is filed in a court of a province under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(5) the order has, from the date it is filed, the same effect as if it had been an order originally made by that court` MEANS
    IF `the order is filed in a court of a province under subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from the date it is filed in a court of a province under subsection (3) or (4)"

-- src:8270 | (6) Where an order has been filed in a court under subsection (3) or (4), it shall not be executed before notice in accordance with subsection 462.41(2) is given to every person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref s 462.371(6) (src:8270)
GIVEN `the order has been filed in a court under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice in accordance with subsection 462.41(2) has been given to every person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(6) the order is barred from being executed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order has been filed in a court under subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order has been filed in a court under subsection (3) or (4)"
    ELSE IF `notice in accordance with subsection 462.41(2) has been given to every person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall not be executed before notice in accordance with subsection 462.41(2) is given" (the notice has been given)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8272 | (7) Section 462.42 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of a person who claims an interest in property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4).
@ref s 462.371(7) (src:8272)
GIVEN `the person claims an interest in property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(7) section 462.42 applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person claims an interest in property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a person who claims an interest in property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)"

-- src:8274 | (8) No person may make an application under section 462.42 in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4) if that person has previously made an application in respect of the same property in another province.
@ref s 462.371(8) (src:8274)
GIVEN `the application is in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has previously made an application in respect of the same property in another province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(8) the person is barred from making an application under section 462.42` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)"
    ELSE IF `the person has previously made an application in respect of the same property in another province`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person has previously made an application in respect of the same property in another province"

-- src:8276 | (9) The finding by a court of a province in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4) as to whether or not an applicant referred to in subsection 462.42(4) is affected by the forfeiture referred to in that subsection or declaring the nature and extent of the interest of the applicant under that subsection is binding on the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the order is entered as a judgment.
@ref s 462.371(9) (src:8276)
GIVEN `a court of a province has made a finding in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the finding is as to whether or not an applicant referred to in subsection 462.42(4) is affected by the forfeiture or declares the nature and extent of the interest of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the order is entered as a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.371(9) the finding is binding on the superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `a court of a province has made a finding in relation to property that is the subject of an order filed under subsection (3) or (4)`
        AND `the finding is as to whether or not an applicant referred to in subsection 462.42(4) is affected by the forfeiture or declares the nature and extent of the interest of the applicant`
        AND `the court is the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the order is entered as a judgment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is binding on the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province where the order is entered as a judgment"

§§ `s 462.38 -- Application for forfeiture; order; deemed absconded`

-- src:8278 | 462.38 (1) Where an information has been laid in respect of a designated offence, the Attorney General may make an application to a judge for an order of forfeiture under subsection (2) in respect of any property.
@ref s 462.38(1) (src:8278)
GIVEN `an information has been laid in respect of an offence that is a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.38(1) the Attorney General may apply to a judge for an order of forfeiture under subsection (2) in respect of any property` MEANS
    `an information has been laid in respect of an offence that is a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("Where an information has been laid in respect of a designated offence"); NOTHING when "designated offence" is itself not covered

-- src:8280 | (2) Subject to sections 462.39 to 462.41, where an application is made to a judge under subsection (1), the judge shall, if the judge is satisfied that
-- src:8281 | (a) any property is, beyond a reasonable doubt, proceeds of crime,
-- src:8282 | (b) that property was obtained through the commission of a designated offence in respect of which proceedings were commenced, and
-- src:8283 | (c) the accused charged with the offence referred to in paragraph (b) has died or absconded,
-- src:8284 | order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law.
@ref s 462.38(2) (src:8280-8284)
GIVEN `an application is made to a judge under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the property is, beyond a reasonable doubt, proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the property was obtained through the commission of a designated offence in respect of which proceedings were commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the accused charged with that offence has died or absconded, by s 462.38(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.38(2) the judge must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application is made to a judge under subsection (1)` AND `the judge is satisfied that the property is, beyond a reasonable doubt, proceeds of crime`
            AND `the judge is satisfied that the property was obtained through the commission of a designated offence in respect of which proceedings were commenced`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an application is made to a judge under subsection (1), the judge shall, if the judge is satisfied that"
    ELSE `the judge is satisfied that the accused charged with that offence has died or absconded, by s 462.38(3)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("if" unmet); NOTHING when the deeming rule of (3) is itself not covered

-- src:8286 | (2.1) An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 462.38(2.1) (src:8286)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.38(2.1) an order may be issued in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- "the period of six months commencing on the day the warrant or summons was issued": the period includes the day of issue, so its last day is the day before the same day six months later.
GIVEN `the day the warrant or summons was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 462.38(3) the last day of the period of six months` MEANS Date (Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the day the warrant or summons was issued`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the warrant or summons was issued` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `the day the warrant or summons was issued`)) MINUS 1)

-- src:8288 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a person shall be deemed to have absconded in connection with a designated offence if
-- src:8289 | (a) an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the person,
-- src:8290 | (b) a warrant for the arrest of the person or a summons in respect of an organization has been issued in relation to that information, and
-- src:8291 | (c) reasonable attempts to arrest the person pursuant to the warrant or to serve the summons have been unsuccessful during the period of six months commencing on the day the warrant or summons was issued, or, in the case of a person who is not or never was in Canada, the person cannot be brought within that period to the jurisdiction in which the warrant or summons was issued,
-- src:8292 | and the person shall be deemed to have so absconded on the last day of that period of six months.
@ref s 462.38(3) (src:8288-8292)
GIVEN `an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant for the arrest of the person or a summons in respect of an organization has been issued in relation to that information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the warrant or summons was issued` IS A DATE
      `reasonable attempts to arrest the person pursuant to the warrant or to serve the summons have been unsuccessful during the period of six months, or the person is not or never was in Canada and cannot be brought within that period to the jurisdiction in which the warrant or summons was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.38(3) the person is deemed to have absconded in connection with the designated offence` MEANS
    IF `an information has been laid alleging the commission of the offence by the person`   -- (a)
        AND `a warrant for the arrest of the person or a summons in respect of an organization has been issued in relation to that information`   -- (b)
        AND `reasonable attempts to arrest the person pursuant to the warrant or to serve the summons have been unsuccessful during the period of six months, or the person is not or never was in Canada and cannot be brought within that period to the jurisdiction in which the warrant or summons was issued`   -- (c)
        AND `the date asked about` AT LEAST `s 462.38(3) the last day of the period of six months` `the day the warrant or summons was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall be deemed to have absconded in connection with a designated offence if"

-- src:8294 | 462.39 For the purpose of subsection 462.37(1) or 462.38(2), the court may infer that property was obtained or derived as a result of the commission of a designated offence where evidence establishes that the value, after the commission of that offence, of all the property of the person alleged to have committed the offence exceeds the value of all the property of that person before the commission of that offence and the court is satisfied that the income of that person from sources unrelated to designated offences committed by that person cannot reasonably account for such an increase in value.
@ref s 462.39 (src:8294)
GIVEN `the purpose is subsection 462.37(1) or 462.38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value, after the commission of the offence, of all the property of the person alleged to have committed the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of all the property of that person before the commission of that offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the court is satisfied that the income of that person from sources unrelated to designated offences committed by that person cannot reasonably account for such an increase in value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.39 the court may infer that the property was obtained or derived as a result of the commission of a designated offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the value, after the commission of the offence, of all the property of the person alleged to have committed the offence` GREATER THAN `the value of all the property of that person before the commission of that offence`
            AND `the court is satisfied that the income of that person from sources unrelated to designated offences committed by that person cannot reasonably account for such an increase in value`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where evidence establishes that the value, after the commission of that offence, of all the property of the person alleged to have committed the offence exceeds the value of all the property of that person before the commission of that offence" (a "where" gate on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the purpose is subsection 462.37(1) or 462.38(2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection 462.37(1) or 462.38(2)"

-- src:8296 | 462.4 A court may,
-- src:8297 | (a) prior to ordering property to be forfeited under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2), and
-- src:8298 | (b) in the case of property in respect of which a restraint order was made under section 462.33, where the order was served in accordance with subsection 462.33(8),
-- src:8299 | set aside any conveyance or transfer of the property that occurred after the seizure of the property or the service of the order under section 462.33, unless the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith.
@ref s 462.4 (src:8296-8299)
GIVEN `before ordering the property to be forfeited under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restraint order was made under section 462.33 in respect of the property and was served in accordance with subsection 462.33(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance or transfer of the property occurred after the seizure of the property or the service of the order under section 462.33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.4 the court may set aside the conveyance or transfer of the property` MEANS
    IF `the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the conveyance or transfer was for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith"
    ELSE IF NOT (`before ordering the property to be forfeited under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)`   -- (a)
                 OR `a restraint order was made under section 462.33 in respect of the property and was served in accordance with subsection 462.33(8)`)   -- (b)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of property in respect of which a restraint order was made under section 462.33, where the order was served in accordance with subsection 462.33(8)" (an occasion gate of the kind "in the case of" and "where" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
         ELSE IF `the conveyance or transfer of the property occurred after the seizure of the property or the service of the order under section 462.33`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "set aside any conveyance or transfer of the property that occurred after the seizure of the property or the service of the order under section 462.33"

§§ `s 462.41 -- Notice; restoration of property`

-- src:8301 | 462.41 (1) Before making an order under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2) in relation to any property, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (2) to be given to and may hear any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref s 462.41(1) (src:8301)
GIVEN `the court is about to make an order under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2) in relation to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears to the court to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.41(1) the court must require notice to be given to the person` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make an order under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2) in relation to the property` AND `the person appears to the court to have a valid interest in the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who, in the opinion of the court, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8303 | (2) A notice shall
-- src:8304 | (a) be given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court;
-- src:8305 | (b) specify the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property; and
-- src:8306 | (c) set out the designated offence charged and a description of the property.
@ref s 462.41(2) (src:8303-8306)
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice sets out the designated offence charged and a description of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.41(2) the notice complies with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court`   -- (a)
        AND `the notice specifies the period that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property`   -- (b)
        AND `the notice sets out the designated offence charged and a description of the property`   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall"

-- src:8308 | (3) Where a court is satisfied that any person, other than
-- src:8309 | (a) a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence, or
-- src:8310 | (b) a person who acquired title to or a right of possession of that property from a person referred to in paragraph (a) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property,
-- src:8311 | is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of any property or any part thereof that would otherwise be forfeited pursuant to subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2) and that the person appears innocent of any complicity in an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or of any collusion in relation to such an offence, the court may order that the property or part thereof be returned to that person.
@ref s 462.41(3) (src:8308-8311)
GIVEN `the person is a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property or any part of it that would otherwise be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears innocent of any complicity in an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or of any collusion in relation to such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.41(3) the court may order that the property or part of it be returned to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence` OR `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any person, other than"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that the person is the lawful owner or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property or any part of it that would otherwise be forfeited` AND `the person appears innocent of any complicity in an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or of any collusion in relation to such an offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court is satisfied that any person"

§§ `s 462.42 -- Application by person claiming interest for relief from forfeiture`

-- src:8313 | 462.42 (1) Any person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2) may, within thirty days after the forfeiture, apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4) unless the person is
-- src:8314 | (a) a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture; or
-- src:8315 | (b) a person who acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from a person referred to in paragraph (a) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property.
@ref s 462.42(1) (src:8313-8315)
GIVEN `the person claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the forfeiture` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies by notice in writing to a judge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(1) the person may apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person who is charged with, or was convicted of, a designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture` OR `the person acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person is"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the date the person applies by notice in writing to a judge` AT LEAST `the date of the forfeiture` AND `the date the person applies by notice in writing to a judge` AT MOST Date (Day `the date of the forfeiture` PLUS 30))
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within thirty days after the forfeiture" (a stated period, the kind "after ...": listed in the fork register, F35)
         ELSE IF `the person claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)"

-- The right of paragraph (1) as a regulative rule: the person MAY apply WITHIN 30 (days from the forfeiture). The core's Party has no constructor for a person claiming an interest in property, so a type of this module's own is declared (NEEDS-CORE.md).
DECLARE `s 462.42 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.42 a person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty`

DECLARE `s 462.42(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.42(1) apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)`

@ref s 462.42(1) (src:8313)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 462.42 party` `s 462.42(1) act`
`s 462.42(1) the right to apply within thirty days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 462.42 a person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty`
    MAY `s 462.42(1) apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:8317 | (2) The judge to whom an application is made under subsection (1) shall fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of filing of the application for the hearing thereof.
@ref s 462.42(2) (src:8317)
GIVEN `the date of filing of the application` IS A DATE
      `the day fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(2) the day fixed for the hearing is not less than thirty days after the date of filing` MEANS
    IF `the day fixed for the hearing` AT LEAST Date (Day `the date of filing of the application` PLUS 30)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall fix a day not less than thirty days after the date of filing of the application for the hearing thereof"

-- src:8319 | (3) An applicant shall serve a notice of the application made under subsection (1) and of the hearing thereof on the Attorney General at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing.
@ref s 462.42(3) (src:8319)
GIVEN `the day fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the day the applicant served a notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(3) the notice was served on the Attorney General at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the day the applicant served a notice of the application and of the hearing on the Attorney General` AT MOST Date (Day `the day fixed for the hearing` MINUS 15)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least fifteen days before the day fixed for the hearing"

-- src:8321 | (4) Where, on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) and appears innocent of any complicity in any designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture or of any collusion in relation to any such offence, the judge may make an order declaring that the interest of the applicant is not affected by the forfeiture and declaring the nature and extent of the interest.
@ref s 462.42(4) (src:8321)
GIVEN `on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant appears innocent of any complicity in any designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture or of any collusion in relation to any such offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(4) the judge may make an order declaring that the interest of the applicant is not affected by the forfeiture` MEANS
    IF `on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1)` AND `the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` AND `the applicant appears innocent of any complicity in any designated offence that resulted in the forfeiture or of any collusion in relation to any such offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the hearing of an application made under subsection (1), the judge is satisfied that the applicant is not a person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)"

-- src:8323 | (5) An applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from an order under subsection (4) and the provisions of Part XXI with respect to procedure on appeals apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to appeals under this subsection.
@ref s 462.42(5) (src:8323)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant or the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is from an order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(5) the person may appeal to the court of appeal` MEANS
    IF `the person is the applicant or the Attorney General` AND `the appeal is from an order under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant or the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal from an order under subsection (4)"

-- src:8325 | (6) The Attorney General shall, on application made to the Attorney General by any person who has obtained an order under subsection (4) and where the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired and any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined,
-- src:8326 | (a) direct that the property or the part thereof to which the interest of the applicant relates be returned to the applicant; or
-- src:8327 | (b) direct that an amount equal to the value of the interest of the applicant, as declared in the order, be paid to the applicant.
@ref s 462.42(6) (src:8325-8327)
GIVEN `the application is made to the Attorney General by a person who has obtained an order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.42(6) the Attorney General must direct that the property be returned to the applicant or that an amount equal to the value of the interest be paid` MEANS
    IF `the application is made to the Attorney General by a person who has obtained an order under subsection (4)` AND `the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired` AND `any appeal from that order taken under subsection (5) has been determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) or (b): the text does not say which; see NOTES.md, fork register
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application made to the Attorney General by any person who has obtained an order under subsection (4) and where the periods with respect to the taking of appeals from that order have expired"

§§ `ss 462.43 to 462.46 -- Residual disposal; appeals; suspension; copies`

-- src:8329 | 462.43 (1) If property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321, a restraint order has been made under section 462.33 in relation to any property or a recognizance has been entered into under paragraph 462.34(4)(a) in relation to any property and a judge, on application made to the judge by the Attorney General or any person having an interest in the property or on the judge’s own motion, after notice given to the Attorney General and any other person having an interest in the property, is satisfied that the property will no longer be required for the purpose of section 462.37, 462.38 or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding, the judge
-- src:8330 | (a) in the case of a restraint order, shall revoke the order;
-- src:8331 | (b) in the case of a recognizance, shall cancel the recognizance; and
-- src:8332 | (c) in the case of property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a),
-- src:8333 | (i) if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is lawful, shall order that it be returned to that person,
-- src:8334 | (ii) if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful and the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known, shall order that it be returned to the lawful owner or the person who is lawfully entitled to its possession, or
-- src:8335 | (iii) if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful and the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is not known, may order that it be forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs, or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law.
@ref s 462.43(1) (src:8329-8335)
GIVEN `property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321, a restraint order has been made under section 462.33 in relation to any property or a recognizance has been entered into under paragraph 462.34(4)(a) in relation to any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge, on application by the Attorney General or any person having an interest in the property or on the judge’s own motion, after notice given to the Attorney General and any other person having an interest in the property, is satisfied that the property will no longer be required for the purpose of section 462.37, 462.38 or any other provision respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` MEANS
    IF `property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321, a restraint order has been made under section 462.33 in relation to any property or a recognizance has been entered into under paragraph 462.34(4)(a) in relation to any property`
        AND `a judge, on application by the Attorney General or any person having an interest in the property or on the judge’s own motion, after notice given to the Attorney General and any other person having an interest in the property, is satisfied that the property will no longer be required for the purpose of section 462.37, 462.38 or any other provision respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321"

@ref s 462.43(1)(a) (src:8330)
GIVEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1)(a) the judge must revoke the restraint order` MEANS
    IF `it is a restraint order`
    THEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when (1) is itself not covered
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a restraint order, shall revoke the order"

@ref s 462.43(1)(b) (src:8331)
GIVEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1)(b) the judge must cancel the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `it is a recognizance`
    THEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when (1) is itself not covered
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a recognizance, shall cancel the recognizance"

@ref s 462.43(1)(c)(i) (src:8332-8333)
GIVEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1)(c)(i) the judge must order that the property be returned to the person from whom it was taken` MEANS
    IF `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` AND `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is lawful`
    THEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when (1) is itself not covered
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is lawful, shall order that it be returned to that person"

@ref s 462.43(1)(c)(ii) (src:8332-8334)
GIVEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1)(c)(ii) the judge must order that the property be returned to the lawful owner or the person lawfully entitled to its possession` MEANS
    IF `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` AND `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful` AND `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known`
    THEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE; NOTHING when (1) is itself not covered
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful and the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known"

@ref s 462.43(1)(c)(iii) (src:8332-8335)
GIVEN `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is not known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(1)(c)(iii) the judge may order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `it is property seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or property under the control of a person appointed under paragraph 462.331(1)(a)` AND `possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful` AND `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is not known`
    THEN (IF `the duty of subsection (1) has arisen, by s 462.43(1) the judge has a duty to act under paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321" (a power named "may": the "if" gate of subsection (1) failing is not the text's no, F36; the "shall" siblings (a), (b), (c)(i) and (ii) keep JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if possession of it by the person from whom it was taken is unlawful and the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is not known, may order that it be forfeited"

-- src:8337 | (2) An order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 462.43(2) (src:8337)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.43(2) an order may be issued in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:8339 | 462.44 Any person who considers that they are aggrieved by an order made under subsection 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43 may appeal from the order as if the order were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, under Part XXI, and that Part applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to such an appeal.
@ref s 462.44 (src:8339)
GIVEN `the person considers that they are aggrieved by an order made under subsection 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.44 the person may appeal from the order as if it were an appeal under Part XXI` MEANS
    IF `the person considers that they are aggrieved by an order made under subsection 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who considers that they are aggrieved by an order made under subsection 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43 may appeal from the order"

-- src:8341 | 462.45 Despite anything in this Part, the operation of an order of forfeiture or restoration of property under subsection 462.34(4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43 is suspended pending
-- src:8342 | (a) any application made in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament that provides for the restoration or forfeiture of such property,
-- src:8343 | (b) any appeal taken from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property, or
-- src:8344 | (c) any other proceeding in which the right of seizure of the property is questioned,
-- src:8345 | and property shall not be disposed of within thirty days after an order of forfeiture is made under any of those provisions.
@ref s 462.45 (src:8341-8345)
GIVEN `the order is an order of forfeiture or restoration of property under subsection 462.34(4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application is pending in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision that provides for the restoration or forfeiture of such property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal is pending from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another proceeding is pending in which the right of seizure of the property is questioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.45 the operation of the order is suspended` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order is an order of forfeiture or restoration of property under subsection 462.34(4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the operation of an order of forfeiture or restoration of property under subsection 462.34(4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43"
    ELSE IF `an application is pending in respect of the property under any of those provisions or any other provision that provides for the restoration or forfeiture of such property`   -- (a)
            OR `an appeal is pending from an order of forfeiture or restoration in respect of the property`   -- (b)
            OR `another proceeding is pending in which the right of seizure of the property is questioned`   -- (c)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is suspended pending"

@ref s 462.45 (src:8345)
GIVEN `the date the order of forfeiture was made` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.45 the property is barred from being disposed of on the date asked about` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the order of forfeiture was made` AND `the date asked about` AT MOST Date (Day `the date the order of forfeiture was made` PLUS 30)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "property shall not be disposed of within thirty days after an order of forfeiture is made"

-- src:8347 | 462.46 (1) If any document is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under subsection 462.34(3) or (4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43, the Attorney General may, before returning the document or complying with the order, cause a copy of the document to be made and retained.
@ref s 462.46(1) (src:8347)
GIVEN `a document is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under subsection 462.34(3) or (4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.46(1) the Attorney General may cause a copy of the document to be made and retained` MEANS
    IF `a document is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under subsection 462.34(3) or (4), 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or section 462.43`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any document is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with"

-- src:8349 | (2) Every copy made under subsection (1) shall, if certified as a true copy by the Attorney General, be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, shall have the same probative force as the original document would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref s 462.46(2) (src:8349)
GIVEN `the copy was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.46(2) the copy is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the copy was made under subsection (1)` AND `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Attorney General`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, if certified as a true copy by the Attorney General, be admissible in evidence"

@ref s 462.46(2) (src:8349)
GIVEN `the copy was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.46(2) the copy has the same probative force as the original document would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way` MEANS
    IF `the copy was made under subsection (1)` AND `the copy is certified as a true copy by the Attorney General` AND NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, shall have the same probative force as the original document would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way"
